{{also|Appendix:Variations of "kun"}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ja|訓読み|tr=kun'yomi}}, literally "meaning reading" (i.e. pronunciation based on meaning).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# In the Japanese language, the pronunciation, or reading, of a [[kanji]] character as a native Japanese word that means what the character represents, contrasted with [[on]].
#: ''Most kanji have two kinds of reading, called "on" and "kun".''

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|kun-yomi}}
* {{l|en|on}}

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|a=knu|unk.}}

