==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/kʏn/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-kun.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|nl|ʏn|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{head|nl|verb form}}

# {{infl of|nl|kunnen||2-inv}}
#: {{ux|nl|'''Kun''' jij iets doen voor mij?|'''Can''' you do something for me?}}

====Usage notes====
* As is usual in Dutch, the ''-t'' is dropped when the pronoun {{m|nl|jij}} / {{m|nl|je}} immediately follows the verb. However, unlike for all other verbs (except {{m|nl|zullen}}), the form that results is not identical to the first-person singular, which is {{m|nl|kan}}. The form {{m|nl|kan}} is also frequently used, by analogy with regular verbs, but it may be considered nonstandard by some.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|nl|kan}}

