==Finnish==

===Etymology===
The singular instructive case of {{m|fi|kuka}}. Originally a lesser used variant of {{m|fi|kuin}}; modern differences between the two were introduced when the language was standardized.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=LL-Q1412 (fin)-Susannaanas-kun.wav}}

===Conjunction===
{{fi-con}}

# [[when]], [[as]], [[while]] {{gloss|temporal: at the same time or instant that}}
#: {{ux|fi|Sain viestisi, '''kun''' olin jo matkalla lentokentälle.|I got your message '''when''' I was already on my way to the airport.}}
#: {{ux|fi|Hän ilmestyi antamaan ohjeita, '''kun''' olin jo saanut työn valmiiksi.|He showed up to give instructions '''when''' I had already finished the job.}}
# [[as soon as]], [[once]]; {{n-g|expresses that the event of the main clause takes place immediately after that of the subclause, often used with the clitic {{m|fi|-han}}}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tulen tapaamaan sinua, '''kun'''(han) saan tämän valmiiksi.|I will come to see you '''as soon as''' I finish this job.}}
# [[as]], [[because]], [[since]] {{gloss|considering that}}
#: {{ux|fi|Hän menetti työpaikkansa, '''kun''' tuli aina myöhässä.|She lost her job '''because''' she was always late.}}
#: {{ux|fi|En voi tulla huomenna, minulla '''kun''' on aamuvuoro.|I cannot come tomorrow '''as''' I have the morning shift.}}
# {{synonym of|fi|kunpa}}

====Derived terms====
